  [1mBritain and Ireland[0m
  7. [1mEddystone (England):[0m The current tower is the fourth on these rocks off Plymouth, and the upper part of the third,
  Smeaton's Tower, was rebuilt on Plymouth Hoe.
  8. [1mBell Rock (Scotland):[0m Robert Stevenson finished it in 1810, and it is the oldest surviving sea-washed lighthouse in
  the world.
  9. [1mSkerryvore (Scotland):[0m Alan Stevenson designed this 48-meter tower, finished in 1844, and it is the tallest
  lighthouse in Scotland.
  10. [1mFlannan Isles (Scotland):[0m It is famous for December 1900, when all three of its keepers vanished without a trace.
  11. [1mSmalls (Wales):[0m In 1801 a keeper there was forced to live alongside his dead colleague's body for months, which
  led to the rule of three keepers per station.
  12. [1mNeist Point (Scotland):[0m This lighthouse sits on the westernmost point of Skye and is one of the most photographed
  in Britain.
  13. [1mBeachy Head (England):[0m The red-and-white tower stands in the sea beneath towering chalk cliffs and was first lit
  in 1902.
  14. [1mFastnet (Ireland):[0m It was nicknamed "Ireland's Teardrop" because it was the last piece of Ireland that many
  emigrants saw on their way to America.

